# The Escape-clear gesture at an idle prompt with a draft, on screen states
# rather than on its 500 ms window (xfx src/tui/gesture.rs:70 CLEAR_WINDOW,
# fx src/core/input/gesture_state.zig:4@481104fd). LAUNCH-SETTLE took this
# gesture out of p5-mcp-menu-old, whose ending timed it with `wait 0.5`, on
# the window's edge; this scenario keeps it, each case well inside the window:
# every key after the first Escape is sent once the hint is on the screen,
# tens of milliseconds into its 500 ms.
# (a) Escape, then Escape inside the window: the second clears the draft.
type alpha one
until shown alpha one
key Escape
until shown esc again to clear
key Escape
until gone esc again to clear
snap a-cleared
# (b) Escape, an edit, Escape inside the window. fx disarms the clear on any
# byte that is not Escape (src/core/app/app_input_runtime.zig:855-859
# @481104fd), so its second Escape arms it again and the draft stays; xfx
# keeps it armed through the edit (gesture.rs:176-188, `other_key`), so its
# second Escape clears the draft. That Escape is left alone a second -- a key
# typed straight after it could be read with it as one Alt key -- and then a
# marker is typed, which both put on the composer (fx after its draft, xfx on
# an empty one) and which takes fx's armed hint down: the snap holds no timer
# on either.
key C-u
type beta two
until shown beta two
key Escape
until shown esc again to clear
type x
key Escape
wait 1
type zz9
until shown zz9
snap b-edit-escape
# Each side's own row, so a side that flips under load (xfx's second Escape
# past its window, which arms the clear again and keeps the draft) fails
# the run instead of turning the pair identical (LAUNCH-SETTLE-F).
xfx: expect b-edit-escape ┃ zz9
fx: expect b-edit-escape beta twoxzz9
# (c) Escape, then the draft deleted. fx takes the hint down at the key; xfx
# keeps it until its 500 ms run out, over an empty composer, which its own
# rule says it should not show (gesture.rs:162-164).
key C-u
until gone zz9
type qq
until shown qq
key Escape
until shown esc again to clear
key BSpace
key BSpace
until gone ┃ q
snap c-deleted
# xfx's hint is still in its window here: a snap past it fails the run.
xfx: expect c-deleted esc again to clear
until gone esc again to clear
snap c-later
